I explored how to use Python's Seaborn and Matplotlib libraries to visualize health data effectively. 
I examined correlation heatmaps, scatter plots, and boxplots to uncover underlying relationships, distributions, and outliers within datasets. 
I learned how to enhance these basic plots by adding explicit axis labels, adjusting figure sizes, and incorporating transparency or regression trendlines for better clarity. 
I also looked at specific code improvements, such as rounding correlation coefficients to two decimal places and applying intuitive diverging color palettes like coolwarm. 
Ultimately, mastering these visualization techniques helps transform raw numbers into clear, professional insights that clearly communicate data trends.
